{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md#1-onboarding-explain-this-repo-to-me-without-reading-every-file","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md","heading":"1. Onboarding / \"explain this repo to me\" — *without reading every file*","level":2,"anchor":"1-onboarding-explain-this-repo-to-me-without-reading-every-file","span":{"start":39,"end":56},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:64330061cc012962d4553b20761f685839c9fea68e634a77e2155c093c7d3015","meta":{"codeRefs":["Use knowledge-crib. First call","to confirm the project is indexed.\nThen","for \"entry point\" and \"request handling\" (limit 8 each).\nFor the top 3 symbols by cluster size, call","with format=markdown\nand give me a 1-paragraph summary of each + how they call each other.\nDon't paste source files — work from the dossiers.","Use","knowledge","crib.","First","call","status","to","confirm","the","project","is","indexed.","Then","query","for","entry","point","and","request","handling","limit","each","For","top","symbols","by","cluster","size","dossier","with","format","markdown","give","me","paragraph","summary","of","how","they","other.","Don","paste","source","files","work","from","dossiers."],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md#2-impact-analysis-before-a-change-the-canonical-crib-prompt","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md","heading":"2. Impact analysis before a change — *the canonical crib prompt*","level":2,"anchor":"2-impact-analysis-before-a-change-the-canonical-crib-prompt","span":{"start":57,"end":73},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:bda6dfb0fcdb7d7c801e72fae6884aa394d9b056361f64fb295c5d848db91140","meta":{"codeRefs":["I'm about to change the signature of AuthService.issue (id sym:src/auth/TokenService.ts#TokenService.issue@L88).\nUse crib","dir=up depth=4, then","dir=down depth=3.\nList the callers that will break (up) and the behavior that changes downstream (down),\neach with its inherited guard chain (cfgPath) so I know the *conditions* under which it fires.\nThen","on the same id to surface any docs I'd need to update.\nKeep it to the EXTRACTED edges only (extractedOnly=true).","**Why:**","returns the AND-chain of guards per affected node — you learn *not just* that","is reachable but that it's reachable *only when","*. That's the rule,\nnot a guess.","about","to","change","the","signature","of","AuthService.issue","id","sym","src/auth/TokenService.ts#TokenService.issue","L88","Use","crib","impact","dir","up","depth","then","down","3.","List","callers","that","will","break","and","behavior","changes","downstream","each","with","its","inherited","guard","chain","cfgPath","so","know","conditions","under","which","it","fires.","Then","describes","on","same","surface","any","docs","need","update.","Keep","EXTRACTED","edges","only","extractedOnly","true"],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md#3-migration-rule-extraction-the-wedge-crib-was-built-for","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md","heading":"3. Migration / rule extraction — *the wedge crib was built for*","level":2,"anchor":"3-migration-rule-extraction-the-wedge-crib-was-built-for","span":{"start":74,"end":92},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:f9d73a37b668004b0ac3ba498c27af73cb1bd55902f639e1392debdd00f4eeb8","meta":{"codeRefs":["Use crib","on sym:claims.pkb#process_claim@L10.\nHand me the rule book: for each terminal action, the AND-chain of conditions that reach it,\nthe source line, and the tables/columns it reads/writes.\nThen do the same with no proc arg (whole system) and group rules by cluster.","Then prove the rebuild matches:","Now point crib at the migrated Java version,","on the equivalent method,\nand diff the two decision tables row-by-row. Flag any rule present in PL/SQL but missing in Java.","Use","crib","extract_rules","on","sym","claims.pkb#process_claim","L10.","Hand","me","the","rule","book","for","each","terminal","action","AND","chain","of","conditions","that","reach","it","source","line","and","tables/columns","reads/writes.","Then","do","same","with","no","proc","arg","whole","system","group","rules","by","cluster.","Now","point","at","migrated","Java","version","equivalent","method","diff","two","decision","tables","row","row.","Flag","any","present","in","PL/SQL","but","missing","Java."],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md#4-deep-dive-one-symbol-the-dossier-prompt-highest-leverage","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md","heading":"4. Deep-dive one symbol — *the dossier prompt (highest leverage)*","level":2,"anchor":"4-deep-dive-one-symbol-the-dossier-prompt-highest-leverage","span":{"start":93,"end":118},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:c3890481b4d2127b248aaef15c38a50520aebf531aca9884dd36159789fcdd37","meta":{"codeRefs":["dossier","Use crib","id=sym:…#assess_application@L39 format=markdown extractedOnly=true.\nThen answer: what error codes can this proc raise, under which conditions, and which\nexception handlers catch them? Which cursor does it iterate and what does the decision table say?","The markdown comes back with fixed sections —",",","— so you can also ask:","From the dossier markdown, extract only the \"## Raises\" and \"## Exception handlers\" sections\ninto a runbook entry. Don't include the source body.","**Paging a large body** (keep the local model in context budget):","Call","with sourceMaxLines=120 (first page). If the source is truncated,\ncall again with sourceStartLine=<the nextLine it returned> for the next page.\nDon't fetch the whole body at once.","Use","crib","id","sym","#assess_application","L39","format","markdown","extractedOnly","true.","Then","answer","what","error","codes","can","this","proc","raise","under","which","conditions","and","exception","handlers","catch","them","Which","cursor","does","it","iterate","the","decision","table","say","From","extract","only","##","Raises","Exception","sections","into","runbook","entry.","Don","include","source","body.","with","sourceMaxLines","120","first","page","If","is","truncated","call","again","sourceStartLine","nextLine","returned","for","next","page.","fetch","whole","body","at","once."],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md#5-debugging-let-crib-narrow-the-blast-radius-before-the-model-reads-anything","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-prompts.md","heading":"5. Debugging — *let crib narrow the blast radius before the model reads anything*","level":2,"anchor":"5-debugging-let-crib-narrow-the-blast-radius-before-the-model-reads-anything","span":{"start":119,"end":134},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:8b4417ba5d54b6083bbb2c18b3b9fb8eef9a82e1f95f0e277e7a88f61e2da0e7","meta":{"codeRefs":["There's a NullPointerException when a loan > 50000 is rejected.\nUse crib:","\"reject loan\" → get the candidate symbols.","the top candidate (extractedOnly=true, markdown).\nFrom the dossier's Decision table + Raises + Exception handlers, tell me which\nraise/error path fires for amount>50000 & credit<700, and which caller feeds it.\nOnly then, if needed,","the exact raising line.","**Why:** the model starts from a structured hypothesis (the decision table already encodes","There","NullPointerException","when","loan","50000","is","rejected.","Use","crib","query","reject","get","the","candidate","symbols.","dossier","top","extractedOnly","true","markdown","From","Decision","table","Raises","Exception","handlers","tell","me","which","raise/error","path","fires","for","amount","credit","700","and","caller","feeds","it.","Only","then","if","needed","source","exact","raising","line."],"links":[]}}
